      "notes": "Update 21 Oct 2026: new file, not an update. Prices are CarDekho New Delhi ex-showroom for the 10 variants (CarDekho Rajauri/Thane pages agree). Conflict: Autocar India and CarDekho launch-day prices were lower (Pack One Above 59 kWh Rs 19.95 lakh, Pack Three Above 79 kWh Rs 29.45 lakh); the current list is used. CarWale Mumbai ranges (Rs 20.65-30.90 lakh) match the current list; CarWale also shows a Rs 16.64 lakh base figure that is inconsistent, so it is not used. Mahindra's own XEV 9S page was not reached. Ranges 521/600/679 km are MIDC Part 1+2 per Autocar (CarWale and CarDekho quote the same numbers without naming the test cycle for each battery). Real-world estimates quoted by Autocar are 400/450/500-550 km, not used. Motor: 228/241/282 bhp and 380 Nm per CarDekho/CarWale; Autocar gives 231/245/286 PS, consistent. Motor kW and motor type were not confirmed, so the type string is generic. DC charging 140/160/180 kW, 20-80% in about 20 min (Autocar and CarWale). AC times are from Autocar: 7.2 kW 8.7/10.2/11.7 h and 11 kW about 6/7/8 h; the 11 kW charger is named 11 kW in Autocar and 11.2 kW for the XEV 9e. No 9S charger add-on variants or prices were confirmed: Rs 50,000 (7.2 kW) and Rs 75,000 (11.2 kW) are from Autocar for the BE 6 and XEV 9e only, so no charger variants were created. Trim wheels and airbags: Pack One Above 18-inch steel with covers and 6 airbags (Autocar); Pack Two Above 18-inch alloy (Autocar) with airbag count not stated; Pack Three and Pack Three Above airbags 7 (Autocar and CarWale FAQ), wheels not stated. Six-seat variants are labelled with captain seats in second row per a news item only. Mileage is null for EVs. Autocar's 'Pack One Above 59 kWh 7-seat' naming is used as printed on CarDekho."
